SUMMARY:Life Long Learning: How Your Medicine Gets Made: Inside the FDA with M. Daniel Gordin\, Ph.D.
DESCRIPTION:Most Americans are unaware of the complex process behind drug approval. Dr. Gordin’s presentation traces a medication’s journey from discovery and testing through FDA review\, highlighting key historical events that shaped modern drug safety regulations. \nAbout the speaker: M. Daniel Gordin\, Ph.D. is a retired regulatory affairs executive with 40+ years in pharmaceutical development\, including FDA service\, and now advises biotechnology startups through SCBio. \nFREE for JCC Member; $15 Nonmember \nRegister Here
URL:https://jccmetrowest.org/event/lll-how-your-medicine-gets-made/
LOCATION:JCC MetroWest | Tepper Hall\, 760 Northfield Ave\, West Orange\, NJ\, 07052\, United States
