SUMMARY:Life Long Learning: The Music of the 70s Through Today with Gary Negbaur
DESCRIPTION:Listen to the music of the 70s through today with Gary Negbaur. This interactive lecture will include live performances and lectures about the singers and songwriters\, as Broadway goes experimental\, jazz gets free\, rock continues to change. \nAbout the speaker: Gary Negbaur is a pianist\, vocalist\, educator\, and composer. He plays Jazz\, Blues\, and American roots music\, combining innovative arrangements of standards with soulful originals. He tours across the country and abroad and composes music for TV\, film\, theater\, and other singers. \nFREE for JCC Member; $15 Nonmember\n \nRegister Here
URL:https://jccmetrowest.org/event/lll-music-of-the-70s/
LOCATION:JCC MetroWest | Tepper Hall\, 760 Northfield Ave\, West Orange\, NJ\, 07052\, United States
